    "text": "To determine how much money Alex has left after his deductions, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the tax deduction.\n2. Calculate the tithe deduction.\n3. Subtract the tax and tithe from Alex's weekly income.\n4. Subtract the weekly water bill from the remaining amount.\n\nLet's start with the tax deduction. Alex's weekly income is $500, and he pays 10% of his income as tax. So, the tax deduction is:\n\\[ 500 \\times 0.10 = 50 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the tithe deduction. Alex gives away 10% of his weekly income as a tithe. So, the tithe deduction is:\n\\[ 500 \\times 0.10 = 50 \\]\n\nNow, we subtract the tax and tithe from Alex's weekly income:\n\\[ 500 - 50 - 50 = 400 \\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the weekly water bill from the remaining amount:\n\\[ 400 - 55 = 345 \\]\n\nTherefore, the amount of money Alex has left is:\n\\[ \\boxed{345} \\]",
